br /> Let my hand guide you to your rightful place<br /> For I am your shepherd<br /> <br /> Blessed are the dead<br /> And now you are among them<br /> Delivered from this mortal coil<br /> <br /> <i>written by Peter Mohrbacher</i><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Are... are those tentacles? Or giant worms? I know biblical angels are kinda Lovecraftian, but there's something deeply disturbing about divine Illithid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1502505#post1502505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> * cue ominous Latin lyrics</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/F_zUDc7bDE4\" target=\"_blank\">Well, happy Ragnarok everybody! Let's drink.</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-08-2023, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T10:02:47-08:00","id":1502520,"title":"","content":"I think that is an accurate depiction of the reaction a new Obrimos has when summoning an Aetherial entity, but as an experienced summoner will tell them: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/lPIXXTtEvzg\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;What is important is not the form of the Entity, but its nature&quot;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T11:46:31-08:00","id":1502530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1502501#post1502501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Very sounds about right. You need to summon enough to provide several uses of the Boon. Which probably requires setting up a specialized summoning area away from prying eyes, investing all the time and effort needed for those summonings, passing multiple Trials and convincing them to grant the Boon (which probably is an ordeal in itself). Then finally dealing with the Acts of Hubris from dimming the light of the Supernal in the world.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I imagine it activating by placing one's hand on the subject, then speaking the Azrael's condemnation of the accused in High Speech. In a moment of deafening silence, a dying breath is heard and a flowing cloud of mana appears, drawing a &lt;Path color&gt; light from the subject before vanishing.<br /> <br /> 1.a- The highest authority of the Lex Magicka in the Consilium would likely be called to conduct an investigation, to confirm if the participants are not becoming Banishers, make sure they were not infected by one and verify if any Rapt were created. The Guardians would be working overtime to deal with the fallout and its very likely an Arrow of the Council of Dragons would be called to shore up the defenses of the Consilium from a highly likely retaliation.<br /> <br /> 2- One of the mage's most significant sympathetic connections will gain a dot in the Dreamer merit (<i>Hurt Locker</i> page 82) to hunt down someone the angel wants dead, losing any accumulated dots once the mission is accomplished. The angel of death is equitable and fair, so there probably is a Supernal justification for it, although it can cause no end of trouble for the summoner. Just like the mage is taking control of another's supernatural life unto themselves, they need to prove they can handle it by becoming responsible for how their actions affect the lives of both people.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3- I find that the <a href=\"https://www.angelarium.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Angelarium</a> is an outstanding source for inspiration on the art and feel of Aetherial angels, in this case:<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/54243095e4b07ee637a9f812/1553200928427-KUU728DO1BTQDUMTJM2E/azrael_seraphim_angel_death_Mohrbacher\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/54243095e4b07ee637a9f812/1553200928427-KUU728DO1BTQDUMTJM2E/azrael_seraphim_angel_death_Mohrbacher\" data-thumb-url=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/54243095e4b07ee637a9f812/1553200928427-KUU728DO1BTQDUMTJM2E/azrael_seraphim_angel_death_Mohrbacher\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> \u200b <b><b>AZRAEL, ANGEL OF DEATH</b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> I have watched you since you were born<br /> I wrote your name in my book as you came into this world<br /> I have had an eye watching your entire life<br /> See now, your name fades with time<br /> And now you shall return from whence you came<br /> Delivered from this mortal coil<br /> <br /> Let this apple take your body from you<br /> Let my hand guide you to your rightful place<br /> For I am your shepherd<br /> <br /> Blessed are the dead<br /> And now you are among them<br /> Delivered from this mortal coil<br /> <br /> <i>written by Peter Mohrbacher</i><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Love the artwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T13:10:21-08:00","id":1502535,"title":"","content":"A thing of note for the first question: Given the odds of a Tetrach being a Prelate, and probably well along with that, they probably more regularly have the aid of Supernal Entities than the average mage, which complicates things.<br /> <br /> My only other real comment on the subject is of course Cornelius's Lament. It might be a very successful attack if pulled off properly, but it's also an idea that can be used both ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T14:47:42-08:00","id":1502541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1502535#post1502535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only other real comment on the subject is of course Cornelius's Lament. It might be a very successful attack if pulled off properly, but it's also an idea that can be used both ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;More angels! MORE! We need to destroy them down to the last man, before they can think to do the same to us!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T15:02:19-08:00","id":1502542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1502541#post1502541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;More angels! MORE! We need to destroy them down to the last man, before they can think to do the same to us!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>More in the vein of &quot;Make sure the strike is meaningfully incisive and have an exit strategy&quot;, but I still laughed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T15:09:18-08:00","id":1502543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1502542#post1502542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More in the vein of &quot;Make sure the strike is meaningfully incisive and have an exit strategy&quot;, but I still laughed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know, but if you have a Consilium willingly enacting this plan, then someone's likely already gone off the deep end. Just because someone is Wise doesn't mean they're... ah... rational.<br /> <br /> Besides, if we're going to start the Mage equivalent of World War III, it may as well be with a bang and a maniacal cackle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T15:49:54-08:00","id":1502544,"title":"","content":"There is also the problem that there are a lot of Supernal entities outside of their summoning circle. If the Seers kill them or they take too long, then the Abyss gets a very big meal, which probably means that Bad Things Happen in that general area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T16:00:51-08:00","id":1502545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1502544#post1502544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the problem that there are a lot of Supernal entities outside of their summoning circle. If the Seers kill them or they take too long, then the Abyss gets a very big meal, which probably means that Bad Things Happen in that general area.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Hubris is probably less of a concern for Seers than the Pentacle, Seers do have a charge against the Abyss, and in this vein, I think the usual &quot;protocol&quot; is rooted in either banishing or binding Supernal entities as opposed to killing them. Not that that mitigates the problem you've pointed out-mistakes happens and decisions get made-but it's a thing that should be kept in mind.<br /> <br /> Getting a Supernal Entity on you is pretty well Mage's Signature case of &quot;Sometimes, all you can do is run.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T13:11:43-08:00","id":1502704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1502545#post1502545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the Hubris is probably less of a concern for Seers than the Pentacle, Seers do have a charge against the Abyss, and in this vein, I think the usual &quot;protocol&quot; is rooted in either banishing or binding Supernal entities as opposed to killing them. Not that that mitigates the problem you've pointed out-mistakes happens and decisions get made-but it's a thing that should be kept in mind.<br /> <br /> Getting a Supernal Entity on you is pretty well Mage's Signature case of &quot;Sometimes, all you can do is run.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure you can bring some sleeper friends and/or paradox to the party... But you have to be willing to finish the job, because they will not stop short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T14:02:39-08:00","id":1502708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1502704#post1502704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure you can bring some sleeper friends and/or paradox to the party... But you have to be willing to finish the job, because they will not stop short.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, the Seers <i>do</i> take a stance against killing Supernal entities, and not even just because of the Hubris against Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Scelesti, on the other hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T06:43:35-08:00","id":1502745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1502708#post1502708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again though, the Seers <i>do</i> take a stance against killing Supernal entities, and not even just because of the Hubris against Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Scelesti, on the other hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am i right in thinking that even if they are about to die a Supernal Being will keep trying to do what it does, just out of a pure stubborn/inflexibility ? It does say a Supernal Being would try to return to the summoning circle when it's time is nearly up, but i presume it would also try to finish its task first (assuming the trial was complete).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T18:07:39-08:00","id":1503413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1502745#post1502745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am i right in thinking that even if they are about to die a Supernal Being will keep trying to do what it does, just out of a pure stubborn/inflexibility ? It does say a Supernal Being would try to return to the summoning circle when it's time is nearly up, but i presume it would also try to finish its task first (assuming the trial was complete).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it can be taken to vary.<br /> <br /> For one thing, I feel as though a lot of information on Supernal Entities should be informed by a distinction in the write-up for Totems of the Primal Wild against spirits of the Shadow, describing the former as possessing autonomy and choice compared to the more nature driven spirits. From that I draw a notion that whatever principle it is an instance of, a thing of the Supernal is still meant to have a genuine sapience, a capacity to make decisions and act according to changing needs.<br /> <br /> You could have some Supernals with principles or bans that make them more strictly adhere to the terms of an agreement or obligation, and some might come across more like forces of nature than thinking creatures with a sense of self-preservation. Still, I think the baseline will be that they place avoiding the Abyss as the top of their hierarchy of needs, prioritising it above all other concerns within reason (like, make a good faith effort to fulfil what they were summoned to do).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T00:10:07-08:00","id":1503432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1503413#post1503413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it can be taken to vary.<br /> <br /> For one thing, I feel as though a lot of information on Supernal Entities should be informed by a distinction in the write-up for Totems of the Primal Wild against spirits of the Shadow, describing the former as possessing autonomy and choice compared to the more nature driven spirits. From that I draw a notion that whatever principle it is an instance of, a thing of the Supernal is still meant to have a genuine sapience, a capacity to make decisions and act according to changing needs.<br /> <br /> You could have some Supernals with principles or bans that make them more strictly adhere to the terms of an agreement or obligation, and some might come across more like forces of nature than thinking creatures with a sense of self-preservation. Still, I think the baseline will be that they place avoiding the Abyss as the top of their hierarchy of needs, prioritising it above all other concerns within reason (like, make a good faith effort to fulfil what they were summoned to do).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i guess a force of nature can be sapient. But what it means to be both is an interesting question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T23:01:09-07:00","id":1509000,"title":"","content":"A bit off-track (and a couple months late), but is it possible for someone who got Azrael-nuked to Awaken again later? They're Sleepwalkers, so it should be possible in theory. <br /> <br /> One could also posit the same question of Timori, although without 2e rules on them its probably a moot point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T02:43:27-07:00","id":1509012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1509000#post1509000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit off-track (and a couple months late), but is it possible for someone who got Azrael-nuked to Awaken again later? They're Sleepwalkers, so it should be possible in theory.<br /> <br /> One could also posit the same question of Timori, although without 2e rules on them its probably a moot point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume they can simply buy a dot of Gnosis in the usual manner (assuming they survive) as they have still signed their name to a watchtower and are thus still metaphysically connected to the supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T03:41:10-07:00","id":1509020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1509012#post1509012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would assume they can simply buy a dot of Gnosis in the usual manner (assuming they survive) as they have still signed their name to a watchtower and are thus still metaphysically connected to the supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Plausible, but I could also see it as being that the ex-mage's gnosis has been shattered and would need to be remade with the help of another (probably different) Watchtower. Or another option: the angel has blocked the mage's gnosis outside of time and it would require either convincing the angel to release it, or convincing another supernal entity to intervene against the original angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T03:47:05-07:00","id":1509021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1509020#post1509020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. Plausible, but I could also see it as being that the ex-mage's gnosis has been shattered and would need to be remade with the help of another (probably different) Watchtower. Or another option: the angel has blocked the mage's gnosis outside of time and it would require either convincing the angel to release it, or convincing another supernal entity to intervene against the original angel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to think it's the former - the latter sounds like a Boon a Remph would bestow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T04:38:18-07:00","id":1509024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502498-angels-of-death?p=1509020#post1509020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. Plausible, but I could also see it as being that the ex-mage's gnosis has been shattered and would need to be remade with the help of another (probably different) Watchtower. Or another option: the angel has blocked the mage's gnosis outside of time and it would require either convincing the angel to release it, or convincing another supernal entity to intervene against the original angel.</div> </div> </div> </div>The correct answer maybe be, whatever is most dramatically appropriate for your game.<br /> <br /> I don't think i want to get all one upping the Supernal beings summoned tyoe competition... Whereas having an NPC wander around with no Gnosis for an good while might be an interesting mystery if the PCs decide to investigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:08:03-07:00","id":1509093,"title":"","content":"I'd assume they could just buy a dot of Gnosis. Awakening a Mage is some kind of Archmage nonsense, so I wouldn't let any spirit of Rank 5 or less actually undo it, which means treating them as if they were just a Mage of Gnosis 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T15:06:46-07:00","id":1509106,"title":"","content":"Personally I think it makes for a more interesting story if the change isn't so easy to undo.<br /> <br /> What if the players are trying to save a Harrowed from execution and their only plan is to have an angel of death remove the harrowed's broken gnosis, though they risk becoming infected themselves if they take too long?<br /> <br /> What if one of the players has had their gnosis blocked in some way by an angel and the only plan the cabal has to restore their friend's magic is to summon the angel and destroy it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}